#' Simulated three-group network data
#'
#' A simulated dataset with known graphs: K = 3 groups, p = 50 variables and
#' n = 150 observations per group, generated by
#' \code{\link{simulate_ssjgl_data}} with scale-free graphs (seed 2022). The
#' groups share a scale-free base graph; each group's graph is the base graph
#' with 5\% of variable pairs flipped, so groups 2 and 3 have more edges than
#' group 1.
#'
#' @format A list with elements
#' \describe{
#'   \item{Y}{List of 3 data matrices, each 150 x 50, with columns
#'     \code{V1, ..., V50}.}
#'   \item{g}{List of 3 true adjacency matrices (50 x 50, 0/1).}
#'   \item{Omega}{List of 3 true precision matrices (50 x 50).}
#' }
#' @source \code{data-raw/simdat.R} in the package sources.
#' @examples
#' str(simdat, max.level = 1)
#' sapply(simdat$g, function(a) sum(a[upper.tri(a)]))  # edges per group
"simdat"
